  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "For an **upper-upscale** hotel positioning strategy in the Caribbean and Latin America, an owner should first consider the major global brands already associated with that scale in industry chain-scale listings and regional hotel portfolios: **Marriott, Westin, Sheraton, Le Méridien, Hyatt Regency, Hyatt, Hilton, Curio Collection by Hilton, and Wyndham**.[2][4]\n\nThe strongest fit usually comes from brands that can bridge *resort demand* and *business/leisure mixed demand* in these markets. In practice, that means:\n\n- **Marriott** — especially **Marriott Hotels**, **Westin**, **Sheraton**, and **Le Méridien**, which are commonly positioned in the upper-upscale tier.[2][4]\n- **Hyatt** — particularly **Hyatt Regency** and **Hyatt**, which are cited as upper-upscale, with Hyatt also extending into the Caribbean through broader luxury and all-inclusive activity.[2][3]\n- **Hilton** — especially **Hilton** and **Curio Collection by Hilton**, both identified as upper-upscale in the cited brand-scale summary.[2]\n- **Wyndham** — including **Wyndham Hotels & Resorts** / **Wyndham Grand** style positioning, which appears in the upper-upscale discussion and has Caribbean presence.[1][2]\n- **LXR Hotels & Resorts** and other high-end soft brands can also be relevant where the asset is distinctive and the owner wants flexible conversion or luxury-adjacent positioning rather than a strict full-service flag.[6]\n\nIf the strategy is specifically **Caribbean and Latin America resort positioning**, the most practical short list is usually:\n\n- **Marriott / Westin / Sheraton / Le Méridien**\n- **Hyatt Regency / Hyatt**\n- **Hilton / Curio Collection by Hilton**\n- **Wyndham**\n- **Accor’s premium/lifestyle options only if the asset is more design-led than traditional full-service**[3][4]\n\nA useful way to think about it is that **upper-upscale** brands in this region work best when they can support either:\n- a **beach/resort leisure** mix, or\n- a **gateway city plus resort** strategy with strong international distribution.[1][3]\n\nIf you want, I can turn this into a **ranked owner consideration list** for the Caribbean and Latin America by **brand strength, development appetite, and likely ADR positioning**.",
